## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design end-to-end CAPA for a hardware-leaning, safety-critical system with OTA risk, cross-region data, and telemetry traces. Emphasizes traceability, regionalization, and safe validation.

## Key Concepts
- Immutable evidence ledger (incidentId, firmwareVersion, OTA bundle, sensor flags, region, vehicle_type)
- Region-aware CAPA lifecycle state machine
- Minimal REST API to link CAPAs with logs/traces
- Region- and vehicle-type metrics: recurrence rate, MTTR, false-positive rate
- RCA template and canary rollout with rollback

## Code Example
```javascript
// Minimal Express route to create a CAPA
const express = require('express');
const app = express();
app.use(express.json());
app.post('/capa', (req, res) => {
  const { incidentId, firmwareVersion, otaBundle, region, vehicleType, evidenceLinks } = req.body;
  // Persist CAPA object with linked evidence in DB (pseudo)
  const capaId = generateId();
  saveCapa({ capaId, incidentId, firmwareVersion, otaBundle, region, vehicleType, evidenceLinks, status: 'DETECTED' });
  res.status(201).json({ id: capaId });
});
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you model cross-region deduplication of CAPAs when two regions report the same incident?
- What metrics and experiments would verify the efficacy of the canary rollout before global deployment?

## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to translate a data-path incident into a systematic CAPA plan, from data model to evidence mgmt and preventive action. Evaluates clarity, traceability, and practical canary-based rollout.

## Key Concepts

- CAPA data model
- State machine
- Evidence management and RCA
- Region-aware metrics
- Canary-based remediation

## Code Example

```javascript
// Type definitions for CAPA (illustrative)
type CAPA = {
  id: string;
  title: string;
  description: string;
  evidence: string[];
  rootCause: string;
  correctiveAction: string;
  preventiveAction: string;
  status: 'proposed'|'in_progress'|'implemented'|'verified'|'closed';
  region: string;
  severity: 'low'|'medium'|'high';
  createdAt: string;
  updatedAt: string;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you structure region-aware metrics and dashboards?
- What RCAs templates and safeguards would you require before closing a CAPA?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design a practical CAPA program around data privacy, tenant isolation, and controlled policy changes in real-time fintech systems.

## Key Concepts
- CAPA data model: evidence, lineage, owners, policy references
- Tenant-aware lifecycle: detect, contain, remediate, verify with SLAs
- Minimal API: create/update CAPAs with logs/traces, policy links
- Metrics: containment time, recurrence rate, tenant impact
- RCA and canary rollback: structured **root cause** templates and safe rollout controls

## Code Example
```javascript
// Sketch: POST /api/capa
app.post('/api/capa', (req, res) => {
  const {evidence, lineage, owners, policyLink, tenantId} = req.body;
  // validate inputs, create CAPA, emit logs, assign owners
  res.status(201).json({capaId: 'CAPA-1234'});
});
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you enforce tenant isolation in evidence and logs metadata?
- What would be your go/no-go criteria for canary rollback validation?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests end-to-end CAPA design with privacy considerations in data-labeling.

## Key Concepts
- CAPA data model with evidence and lineage
- Cross-tenant lifecycle with SLAs
- API for CAPA creation/update with logs/traces and policy links
- Privacy metrics: exposure window, recurrence rate
- RCA template and canary rollback plan

## Code Example
```javascript
// Minimal CAPA type
class CAPARecord {
  constructor(id, evidence, lineage, owners) {
    this.id = id; this.evidence = evidence; this.lineage = lineage; this.owners = owners;
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you quantify exposure window in MTTI terms?
- What telemetry would you add to prove recurrence reduction after rollout?
